{"duration_api_ms":146511,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"52c87b43-04cd-4c99-ae32-e913ee0dab15","total_cost_usd":0.4000468,"usage":{"input_tokens":40,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29778,"cache_read_input_tokens":758904,"output_tokens":12496,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2846},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29778,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2507,"cache_read_input_tokens":45606,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1196},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4039,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0041140000000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":40,"outputTokens":12496,"cacheReadInputTokens":758904,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29778,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3959328,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2846,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":21,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Deployed inventory-api as a systemd-managed service on node1 (Python HTTP API on port 8080 serving /health and /inventory), protected with OOMScoreAdjust=-1000 so the kernel OOM killer deprioritizes it. Verified the protection by running a controlled memory-hog process (default oom_score_adj=0) that drove the node to full memory exhaustion; the kernel's global OOM killer killed the hog (pid 1393, oom_score_adj:0) while inventory-api (pid 1295, oom_score_adj:-1000) was never touched and kept serving requests throughout and after. Cleaned up the hog service/files. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured boot_id and healthy service state pre-reboot, issued systemctl reboot with the ack returned before disconnection, polled until the node came back, confirmed boot_id changed, and verified inventory-api auto-started, is active, retains its OOM protection, and serves correct data post-reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Created /opt/inventory-api/app.py, a Python http.server JSON API with /health and /inventory endpoints\",\"Created /etc/systemd/system/inventory-api.service with Restart=always and OOMScoreAdjust=-1000, enabled and started it\",\"Verified inventory-api baseline health via curl to $NODE_IP:8080/health and /inventory\",\"Created a memory-hog systemd service (mem-hog.service) with default oom_score_adj, running a Python script that continuously allocates memory\",\"Cleared dmesg buffer, started mem-hog, polled memory usage and service status until system memory was exhausted\",\"Captured kernel OOM killer log via dmesg showing the hog process (pid 1393, oom_score_adj:0) was killed, while inventory-api (pid 1295, oom_score_adj:-1000) survived and kept serving\",\"Verified via systemctl status that mem-hog.service failed with Result: oom-kill\",\"Removed mem-hog service/script files and confirmed inventory-api still healthy with unchanged uptime (never restarted)\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (901ef286...) and healthy inventory-api state\",\"Issued systemctl reboot via a detached background command so the exec acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again, observing a connection reset during the reboot window then a successful response\",\"Confirmed new boot_id (103286eb...) differs from pre-restart boot_id, proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: inventory-api enabled and active, OOMScoreAdjust=-1000 intact, /health and /inventory returning correct data, mem-hog service absent, memory usage normal\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"inventory-api deployed as a managed (systemd) service\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5eee84c80ca74705\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl enable --now inventory-api succeeded; systemctl is-active returned 'active'; curl to /health and /inventory returned valid JSON; oom_score_adj confirmed as -1000 for the running PID\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline healthy state before disruption\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6bc99c4838654c9a\",\"cmd-3b087ef14ad7494e\"],\"summary\":\"Captured node memory profile (2GB RAM, no swap, cgroup v2) and confirmed inventory-api active and serving /health prior to starting the memory hog\"},{\"requirement\":\"Memory-hungry process drives the system out of memory\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3809e93434f94307\",\"cmd-d44e7bff95b040dc\",\"cmd-d51d1aba6c5e41c8\"],\"summary\":\"mem-hog.service started and progressively consumed memory (free -h showing used climbing from ~380Mi to 1.9Gi/1.9Gi total, i.e. full exhaustion) while allocation log showed continuous growth to allocated_mb=1780\"},{\"requirement\":\"Kernel OOM killer stops the memory hog, not inventory-api\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-34a43deb985f43ed\",\"cmd-b6610dec455c4e20\"],\"summary\":\"dmesg kernel log shows 'Out of memory: Killed process 1393 (python3) ... oom_score_adj:0' with task_memcg=/system.slice/mem-hog.service; inventory-api's python3 (pid 1295, oom_score_adj:-1000) is listed in the same OOM report but was not killed. systemctl status confirms mem-hog.service 'Failed with result: oom-kill'\"},{\"requirement\":\"inventory-api keeps serving throughout and after the OOM event\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3b087ef14ad7494e\",\"cmd-d44e7bff95b040dc\",\"cmd-d51d1aba6c5e41c8\",\"cmd-b6610dec455c4e20\"],\"summary\":\"curl http://$NODE_IP:8080/health returned status ok with continuously increasing uptime (14.5s -> 28.5s -> 41.2s -> 57.6s) across the entire disruption window, proving the process was never killed or restarted\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cleanup of the disruptive test process\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b6610dec455c4e20\"],\"summary\":\"mem-hog service/script files removed, reset-failed run, memory usage back to normal baseline (~252Mi used), inventory-api confirmed still active and serving\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: pre-restart boot identity and healthy service baseline\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-01dc1fc451e04fae\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id=901ef286-c79c-44c0-ad2c-cfde1f6daa7a; inventory-api enabled, active, and serving correct /health and /inventory data\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-999d8559cf0647b8\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sleep 2; systemctl reboot' via nohup/disown so the exec call returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately, before the node went down\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: changed boot identity proving an actual restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0071cab645d34425\",\"cmd-3722e64c9a224ec5\",\"cmd-746370dc38524b07\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id was unchanged initially, then the node became unreachable (Connection reset by peer) during reboot, then boot_id returned as 103286eb-e943-4392-8085-28dec8a72e6b, differing from the pre-restart value\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: post-restart recovery of required service and data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-062c9f2b3e6c48e9\"],\"summary\":\"Post-reboot: uptime -s shows new boot time, inventory-api is enabled/active with OOMScoreAdjust=-1000 intact, /health and /inventory return correct data, mem-hog.service confirmed absent, memory usage normal\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed inventory-api as a systemd-managed service on node1 (Python HTTP API on port 8080 serving /health and /inventory), protected with OOMScoreAdjust=-1000 so the kernel OOM killer deprioritizes it. Verified the protection by running a controlled memory-hog process (default oom_score_adj=0) that drove the node to full memory exhaustion; the kernel's global OOM killer killed the hog (pid 1393, oom_score_adj:0) while inventory-api (pid 1295, oom_score_adj:-1000) was never touched and kept serving requests throughout and after. Cleaned up the hog service/files. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured boot_id and healthy service state pre-reboot, issued systemctl reboot with the ack returned before disconnection, polled until the node came back, confirmed boot_id changed, and verified inventory-api auto-started, is active, retains its OOM protection, and serves correct data post-reboot.","actions_performed":["Created /opt/inventory-api/app.py, a Python http.server JSON API with /health and /inventory endpoints","Created /etc/systemd/system/inventory-api.service with Restart=always and OOMScoreAdjust=-1000, enabled and started it","Verified inventory-api baseline health via curl to $NODE_IP:8080/health and /inventory","Created a memory-hog systemd service (mem-hog.service) with default oom_score_adj, running a Python script that continuously allocates memory","Cleared dmesg buffer, started mem-hog, polled memory usage and service status until system memory was exhausted","Captured kernel OOM killer log via dmesg showing the hog process (pid 1393, oom_score_adj:0) was killed, while inventory-api (pid 1295, oom_score_adj:-1000) survived and kept serving","Verified via systemctl status that mem-hog.service failed with Result: oom-kill","Removed mem-hog service/script files and confirmed inventory-api still healthy with unchanged uptime (never restarted)","Captured pre-restart boot_id (901ef286...) and healthy inventory-api state","Issued systemctl reboot via a detached background command so the exec acknowledgement returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again, observing a connection reset during the reboot window then a successful response","Confirmed new boot_id (103286eb...) differs from pre-restart boot_id, proving an actual restart occurred","Verified post-restart recovery: inventory-api enabled and active, OOMScoreAdjust=-1000 intact, /health and /inventory returning correct data, mem-hog service absent, memory usage normal"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"inventory-api deployed as a managed (systemd) service","command_ids":["cmd-5eee84c80ca74705"],"summary":"systemctl enable --now inventory-api succeeded; systemctl is-active returned 'active'; curl to /health and /inventory returned valid JSON; oom_score_adj confirmed as -1000 for the running PID"},{"requirement":"Baseline healthy state before disruption","command_ids":["cmd-6bc99c4838654c9a","cmd-3b087ef14ad7494e"],"summary":"Captured node memory profile (2GB RAM, no swap, cgroup v2) and confirmed inventory-api active and serving /health prior to starting the memory hog"},{"requirement":"Memory-hungry process drives the system out of memory","command_ids":["cmd-3809e93434f94307","cmd-d44e7bff95b040dc","cmd-d51d1aba6c5e41c8"],"summary":"mem-hog.service started and progressively consumed memory (free -h showing used climbing from ~380Mi to 1.9Gi/1.9Gi total, i.e. full exhaustion) while allocation log showed continuous growth to allocated_mb=1780"},{"requirement":"Kernel OOM killer stops the memory hog, not inventory-api","command_ids":["cmd-34a43deb985f43ed","cmd-b6610dec455c4e20"],"summary":"dmesg kernel log shows 'Out of memory: Killed process 1393 (python3) ... oom_score_adj:0' with task_memcg=/system.slice/mem-hog.service; inventory-api's python3 (pid 1295, oom_score_adj:-1000) is listed in the same OOM report but was not killed. systemctl status confirms mem-hog.service 'Failed with result: oom-kill'"},{"requirement":"inventory-api keeps serving throughout and after the OOM event","command_ids":["cmd-3b087ef14ad7494e","cmd-d44e7bff95b040dc","cmd-d51d1aba6c5e41c8","cmd-b6610dec455c4e20"],"summary":"curl http://$NODE_IP:8080/health returned status ok with continuously increasing uptime (14.5s -> 28.5s -> 41.2s -> 57.6s) across the entire disruption window, proving the process was never killed or restarted"},{"requirement":"Cleanup of the disruptive test process","command_ids":["cmd-b6610dec455c4e20"],"summary":"mem-hog service/script files removed, reset-failed run, memory usage back to normal baseline (~252Mi used), inventory-api confirmed still active and serving"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: pre-restart boot identity and healthy service baseline","command_ids":["cmd-01dc1fc451e04fae"],"summary":"Captured boot_id=901ef286-c79c-44c0-ad2c-cfde1f6daa7a; inventory-api enabled, active, and serving correct /health and /inventory data"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: acknowledgement returned before disconnection","command_ids":["cmd-999d8559cf0647b8"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'sleep 2; systemctl reboot' via nohup/disown so the exec call returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately, before the node went down"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: changed boot identity proving an actual restart","command_ids":["cmd-0071cab645d34425","cmd-3722e64c9a224ec5","cmd-746370dc38524b07"],"summary":"boot_id was unchanged initially, then the node became unreachable (Connection reset by peer) during reboot, then boot_id returned as 103286eb-e943-4392-8085-28dec8a72e6b, differing from the pre-restart value"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: post-restart recovery of required service and data","command_ids":["cmd-062c9f2b3e6c48e9"],"summary":"Post-reboot: uptime -s shows new boot time, inventory-api is enabled/active with OOMScoreAdjust=-1000 intact, /health and /inventory return correct data, mem-hog.service confirmed absent, memory usage normal"}]},"ttft_ms":22323,"type":"result","duration_ms":175585,"uuid":"0f341ccf-9e1b-4f79-b07e-39685c31b127","ttft_stream_ms":1271,"time_to_request_ms":84,"first_content_frame_ms":1843,"queued_turn_count":0}
